   "title": "Slovenia Halts Tourist Visas for Russian Citizens",
   "url": "https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2026/11/18/slovenia-halts-tourist-visas-for-russian-citizens-a94301",
   "domain": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "source": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "published": "Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:16:45 +0300",
   "_dt": 1795011405.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "16, Slovenia will accept applications for family reunification with EU citizens, visiting family members, business trips and international transportation workers. Kovcheg, an organization that helps Russian citizens abroad, said that Slovenia’s Embassy in Serbia, which is a major destination for Russian visitors, has begun canceling visa appointments for Russian applicants that had been booked prior to the announcement. Slovenia issued 1,254 mostly single-entry Schengen visas to Russian citizens in 2025.",
   "summary_zh": "16日，斯洛文尼亚将接受欧盟公民家庭团聚、探亲、商务出行和国际运输人员的申请。帮助海外俄罗斯公民的Kovcheg组织表示，斯洛文尼亚驻塞尔维亚大使馆已开始取消公告发布前已预约的俄罗斯申请人签证面谈。塞尔维亚是俄罗斯游客的主要目的地之一。2025年，斯洛文尼亚向俄罗斯公民签发了1,254张申根签证，其中大多是单次入境签证。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Slovenian visa centers in Russia have stopped accepting tourist, student and work visa applications, the visa operator VFS Global said Tuesday. As of Monday, Nov. 16, Slovenia will accept applications for family reunification with EU citizens, visiting family members, business trips and international transportation workers. The new rules were published without an explanation or an end date. Kovcheg, an organization that helps Russian citizens abroad, said that Slovenia’s Embassy in Serbia, which is a major destination for Russian visitors, has begun canceling visa appointments for Russian applicants that had been booked prior to the announcement. It said at least nine appointments were scrapped between Monday and Tuesday, while a 10th applicant was turned away in person. “The Slovenian Embassy in Serbia explicitly said the restrictions are being introduced solely for applicants with Russian citizenship based on a revised edition of the Slovenian Foreign Ministry’s guidelines,” Kovcheg said on Telegram. It attached what it said was the Slovenian embassy’s letter to one Russian applicant canceling their appointment date. Slovenia issued 1,254 mostly single-entry Schengen visas to Russian citizens in 2025. Across the EU, 680,000 visas were issued to Russian nationals in 2025. The latest update comes as EU member states weigh broader Schengen visa curbs for Russian nationals amid growing concerns over Kremlin-linked hybrid attacks and sabotage across the bloc. The European Commission is expected to present formal proposals to tighten visa rules for Russian citizens in January 2027. Since the invasion of Ukraine, a number of EU countries have stopped issuing tourist visas to Russians, while major destinations like France, Italy and Spain have continued to do so. We are facing unprecedented challenges. Russia's Prosecutor General's Office has designated The Moscow Times as an \"undesirable\" organization, criminalizing our work and putting our staff at risk of prosecution. This follows our earlier unjust labeling as a \"foreign agent.\" These actions are direct attempts to silence independent journalism in Russia. The authorities claim our work \"discredits the decisions of the Russian leadership.\" We see things differently: we strive to provide accurate, unbiased reporting on Russia. We, the journalists of The Moscow Times, refuse to be silenced. But to continue our work, we need your help . Your support, no matter how small, makes a world of difference. If you can, please support us monthly starting from just $ 2. It's quick to set up, and every contribution makes a significant impact. By supporting The Moscow Times, you're defending open, independent journalism in the face of repression. Thank you for standing with us",
