   "_dt": 1795008929.0,
   "ageDays": 0.07,
   "summary": "Vice President Professor Naana Jane Opoku-Agyemang has urged MTN Ghana to increase investment in network quality, customer experience and connectivity in underserved communities as the country works to widen access to digital services. Speaking at the MTN Ghana @30 Stakeholders Dinner in Accra, Professor Opoku-Agyemang said access to reliable and affordable connectivity should not depend on where a person lives.",
   "summary_zh": "副总统纳娜·简·奥波库-阿吉曼教授敦促MTN Ghana加大投资，改善网络质量、客户体验和服务不足社区的连接条件，同时加纳正努力扩大数字服务覆盖范围。奥波库-阿吉曼教授在阿克拉举行的MTN Ghana成立30周年利益相关方晚宴上表示，人们能否获得可靠且负担得起的网络连接，不应取决于其居住地。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "Vice President Professor Naana Jane Opoku-Agyemang has urged MTN Ghana to increase investment in network quality, customer experience and connectivity in underserved communities as the country works to widen access to digital services. She said sustained investment in telecommunications infrastructure was critical to ensuring that more Ghanaians benefit from opportunities in the country's growing digital economy. Speaking at the MTN Ghana @30 Stakeholders Dinner in Accra, Professor Opoku-Agyemang said access to reliable and affordable connectivity should not depend on where a person lives. She disclosed that the government had allocated GH¢45 million in the 2027 Budget for rural telephony projects to extend telecommunications services to communities with limited access",
