   "title": "Vice President urges stronger cybersecurity to protect mobile money users",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/vice-president-urges-stronger-cybersecurity-to-protect-mobile-money-users/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:31:00 +0000",
   "_dt": 1795008660.0,
   "ageDays": 0.07,
   "summary": "Vice President Professor Naana Jane Opoku-Agyemang has called for stronger data protection, cybersecurity and accountability in Ghana’s digital financial services sector to safeguard mobile money users against fraud and other risks. She said the rapid growth of mobile money and other digital financial services must be matched with reliable security systems to sustain public confidence in electronic transactions.",
   "summary_zh": "副总统纳纳·简·奥波库-阿吉芒教授呼吁加强加纳数字金融服务业的数据保护、网络安全和问责机制，保护移动支付用户免受欺诈及其他风险侵害。她表示，移动支付及其他数字金融服务的快速增长必须与可靠的安全系统相匹配，才能维持公众对电子交易的信心。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "Vice President Professor Naana Jane Opoku-Agyemang has called for stronger data protection, cybersecurity and accountability in Ghana’s digital financial services sector to safeguard mobile money users against fraud and other risks. She said the rapid growth of mobile money and other digital financial services must be matched with reliable security systems to sustain public confidence in electronic transactions. Speaking at the MTN Ghana @30 Stakeholders Dinner in Accra, Professor Opoku-Agyemang acknowledged the role of mobile money in expanding financial inclusion, particularly for small businesses, families and people previously underserved by traditional banking services. She said the service had made it easier for businesses to receive payments and for families to transfer money across the country without relying on costly financial infrastructure",
