   "title": "Oti Regional Minister highlights government development projects",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/oti-regional-minister-highlights-government-development-projects/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:13:00 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794892380.0,
   "ageDays": 1.42,
   "summary": "John Kwadwo Gyapong, Oti Regional Minister, has highlighted development projects being undertaken by the John Dramani Mahama-led government in the region, urging residents to acknowledge efforts to improve infrastructure and social services. The Regional Minister said the projects demonstrated the government’s commitment to fulfilling its development promises, adding that the people of the region had reasons to appreciate the interventions.",
   "summary_zh": "Oti地区部长John Kwadwo Gyapong重点介绍了由John Dramani Mahama领导的政府正在该地区实施的发展项目，敦促居民认可政府在改善基础设施和社会服务方面付出的努力。该地区部长表示，这些项目体现了政府履行发展承诺的决心，并补充说，该地区人民有理由对这些干预措施表示肯定。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "John Kwadwo Gyapong, Oti Regional Minister, has highlighted development projects being undertaken by the John Dramani Mahama-led government in the region, urging residents to acknowledge efforts to improve infrastructure and social services. He mentioned road projects under the government’s Big Push initiative, including the Dodo-Pepesu-Nkwanta, Nkwanta-Kpassa, Nkwanta-Dambai and Okadjakrom-Kwamekrom roads, describing them as significant interventions expected to improve transportation, connectivity and economic activities across the region. Mr Gyapong made these remarks during a media engagement on the sidelines of the National Democratic Congress (NDC) Oti Regional Executive Elections held at the Bueman Senior High School (BUSEC) in Jasikan on November 14. He also cited the proposed university at Jasikan, the Oti Regional Hospital project, the establishment of 24-Hour Economy Markets across the region, the proposed airport at Dambai and the Dambai Bridge project as other major development initiatives. He said the President was expected to cut the sod for the Oti Regional Hospital project soon, expressing optimism that its construction would improve access to healthcare services and reduce the challenges residents faced in seeking specialised medical attention. The Regional Minister said the projects demonstrated the government’s commitment to fulfilling its development promises, adding that the people of the region had reasons to appreciate the interventions. According to him, the government had moved beyond promises to implementing projects that would address critical infrastructure and development needs in the region. He further disclosed that several other interventions, including the construction of school blocks, Community-based Health Planning and Services (CHPS) compounds and water supply facilities, were being undertaken across the region’s nine districts. Mr Gyapong therefore challenged journalists to visit the various communities to independently assess the projects and report on their implementation and impact on residents. He said media practitioners had an important responsibility to provide accurate information on development initiatives and their benefits to the people. He urged the media to give adequate attention to ongoing development projects in the region to enable residents to appreciate the interventions and hold relevant authorities accountable for their implementation",
