   "title": "Indian enrolment for us higher education fell notes report president donald trump us visa post study work opt 101794794680857",
   "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/indian-enrolment-for-us-higher-education-fell-notes-report-president-donald-trump-us-visa-post-study-work-opt-101794794680857.html",
   "domain": "hindustantimes.com",
   "source": "hindustantimes.com",
   "published": "Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:45:46 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794795346.0,
   "ageDays": 2.54,
   "summary": "According to the report, titled Open Doors Report on International Educational Exchange, the latest decline was driven largely by a 34% drop in Indian students pursuing graduate programmes, whose numbers fell from 177,892 in 2024–25 to 116,609. However, the number of Indian students participating in OPT, which allows international graduates to gain work experience in the US after completing their degrees, rose 27% to 182,201.",
   "summary_zh": "据题为《国际教育交流开放之门报告》的报告称，最近的下降主要是因为攻读研究生课程的印度学生人数大幅减少34%，从2024—2025年的177,892人降至116,609人。不过，参与OPT的印度学生人数增加了27%，达到182,201人。OPT允许国际毕业生在完成学位后赴美国积累工作经验。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "It was released to the public on Monday. HT was given early access to a copy of the report. According to the report, titled Open Doors Report on International Educational Exchange, the latest decline was driven largely by a 34% drop in Indian students pursuing graduate programmes, whose numbers fell from 177,892 in 2024–25 to 116,609. Undergraduate enrolments also dipped marginally to 39,711 from 40,135. However, the number of Indian students participating in OPT, which allows international graduates to gain work experience in the US after completing their degrees, rose 27% to 182,201. Across all academic levels, 57% of international students were enrolled in science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) fields. Mathematics and computer science, with 286,168 students, and engineering, with 214,193, were the most popular fields. Meanwhile, OPT participation among international students rose 14% to 335,785. The number of new international students — those enrolling at a US institution for the first time — fell 18% to 228,123. The report’s fall 2026 snapshot, based on responses from more than 800 US higher education institutions, points to a further slowdown. Overall international student numbers declined 9%, with new enrolments falling 15%. Graduate enrolments dropped 15%, undergraduate numbers 3% and OPT participation 6%. The decline comes amid tightening US immigration measures and visa-related uncertainties. HT reported on October 23 that arrivals of Indian students in the US on F and M category visas had plunged 39% year-on-year to 25,321 in August 2026. Experts and study-abroad consultants cited stricter visa screening, delays in appointments and processing, higher rejection rates and uncertainty over post-study employment opportunities, including OPT, as factors affecting student mobility",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
